    "title": "Acceptable Use Policy",
    "requiresAcceptance": true,
    "summary": "First version for the AIGen Hub beta.",
    "bodyMd": "# Acceptable Use Policy\n\nThis policy applies to everyone who uses AIGen Hub. Breaking it may lead to suspension under the [Terms of Service](/legal/terms).\n\n## 1. Messaging rules\n\n- Send marketing messages only to people who agreed to receive them, and keep proof of that agreement.\n- Honour every request to stop, at once.\n- Follow the policies of each platform you connect, including the WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, Instagram and Facebook policies, TikTok and Telegram rules.\n- WhatsApp may not be used for a general-purpose AI chatbot. The AI assistant in AIGen Hub must stay a support for your own business, and a person must always be reachable.\n- Do not pretend to be another person or business.\n\n## 2. Content you must not send or store\n\n- Anything unlawful in Malaysia or in your customer's country.\n- Scams, phishing, pyramid schemes or misleading offers.\n- Malware or links to it.\n- Harassment, threats, hate speech, or content that sexualises minors.\n- Personal data you have no right to use.\n\n## 3. Businesses we do not serve\n\nUnlicensed gambling, unlicensed financial services or money lending, illegal drugs, weapons, adult services, counterfeit goods, and any business that needs a licence it does not have.\n\n## 4. Security and fair use\n\n- Do not try to access another company's data or bypass limits.\n- Do not test AIGen Hub's security without our written permission. Report weaknesses to hello@aigen.my.\n- Do not overload the service, scrape it, or resell it without an agreement with us.\n\n## 5. What we do\n\nWe may remove content, pause a channel, or suspend an account that breaks this policy. Where reasonable, we will tell you first and give you a chance to fix the problem.\n\n*This document is a draft for the AIGen Hub beta and is being reviewed by a Malaysian lawyer.*\n",
    "html": "<h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1>\n<p>This policy applies to everyone who uses AIGen Hub. Breaking it may lead to suspension under the <a href=\"/legal/terms\">Terms of Service</a>.</p>\n<h2>1. Messaging rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Send marketing messages only to people who agreed to receive them, and keep proof of that agreement.</li>\n<li>Honour every request to stop, at once.</li>\n<li>Follow the policies of each platform you connect, including the WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, Instagram and Facebook policies, TikTok and Telegram rules.</li>\n<li>WhatsApp may not be used for a general-purpose AI chatbot. The AI assistant in AIGen Hub must stay a support for your own business, and a person must always be reachable.</li>\n<li>Do not pretend to be another person or business.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Content you must not send or store</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Anything unlawful in Malaysia or in your customer&#39;s country.</li>\n<li>Scams, phishing, pyramid schemes or misleading offers.</li>\n<li>Malware or links to it.</li>\n<li>Harassment, threats, hate speech, or content that sexualises minors.</li>\n<li>Personal data you have no right to use.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Businesses we do not serve</h2>\n<p>Unlicensed gambling, unlicensed financial services or money lending, illegal drugs, weapons, adult services, counterfeit goods, and any business that needs a licence it does not have.</p>\n<h2>4. Security and fair use</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Do not try to access another company&#39;s data or bypass limits.</li>\n<li>Do not test AIGen Hub&#39;s security without our written permission. Report weaknesses to <a href=\"mailto:hello@aigen.my\">hello@aigen.my</a>.</li>\n<li>Do not overload the service, scrape it, or resell it without an agreement with us.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5. What we do</h2>\n<p>We may remove content, pause a channel, or suspend an account that breaks this policy. Where reasonable, we will tell you first and give you a chance to fix the problem.</p>\n<p><em>This document is a draft for the AIGen Hub beta and is being reviewed by a Malaysian lawyer.</em></p>\n",
